.TH SDL_HINT_WINDOW_ALLOW_TOPMOST 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WINDOW_ALLOW_TOPMOST \- If set to \(dq0\(dq then never set the top-most flag on an SDL Window even if the application requests it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WINDOW_ALLOW_TOPMOST \(dqSDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_TOPMOST\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a debugging aid for developers and not expected to be used by end users\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: don\(aqt allow topmost
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: allow topmost (default)
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

